   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Pronombres posesivos",
    "@en": "Posessive pronouns"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "El pronombre posesivo sustituye al grupo «posesivo + sustantivo»: **my keys → mine**, **your keys → yours**, **his keys → his**, **her keys → hers**, **our keys → ours**, **their keys → theirs**.",
     "@en": "The possessive pronoun replaces the «posesivo + sustantivo» group: **my keys → mine**, **your keys → yours**, **his keys → his**, **her keys → hers**, **our keys → ours**, **their keys → theirs**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Va solo, sin sustantivo después: **Those keys are mine**, no *mine keys*.",
     "@en": "It goes alone, without noun after: **Those keys are mine**, no * mine keys *."
    },
    {
     "@es": "La forma inglesa depende de quién posee el objeto, no de su género o número. En español sí concuerda: **Those keys are mine** = «Esas llaves son mías».",
     "@en": "The English form depends on who owns the object, not on its gender or number. In Spanish it does agree: **Those keys are mine** = «Those keys are mine.»."
    }
   ]
  },
